{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NGD3krkscuSWbJ8JWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Browser suite, one test: the same pair for a checkbox's `checked`, where the visitor toggles it, an unrelated re-render leaves it, and a changed bound value wins.\n[x] Browser suite: a `select` created with a bound `value` has the matching option selected immediately after mount.\n[x] Browser suite: binding `null` to `value` yields an empty string property.\n[x] Browser suite: `String()` of the same markup still contains the control values as attributes.\n\nThe browser templater now writes `value`, `checked` and `selected` on form controls as DOM properties. It only writes when the bound value has changed since its last write. So an unrelated re-render keeps what the visitor typed, and a changed bound value still replaces it. The full browser suite passes (308/308), and so do lint and the SSR suite. Everything is committed except `.nightralph/notes.md`.\n\n**Changes in `src/htm.browser.ts`:**\n- `_setAttr` handles the three properties on `input`, `textarea`, `select` and `option`. A `WeakMap` holds the last value bound to each element, and values are compared with `Object.is`. `value` writes `''` for `null`/`undefined` and the string form otherwise; `checked` and `selected` write a boolean.\n- `_create` and `_patch` now build children before binding attributes, for every element, so a `select`'s value is set after its options exist. Doing this only for `select` would have added bytes.\n- The `String()` path is unchanged.\n\n**Tests:** I ran each new test against the old source. The value, input edit, checkbox and select tests fail there, so they really test the change. The `null` and `String()` tests also pass on the old source, because the old attribute path already behaved that way for them. They guard against regressions rather than drive new code.\n\n**Things you should know:**\n- **Size limit raised:** the browser templater bundle grew by about 110 B and went over its 4.6 kB limit. I trimmed what I could, then raised the limit to 4.7 kB (measured 4.66 kB, rounded up to the next 0.05 kB as the spec says), with a comment in `.size-limit.js`.\n- **Adopt path still writes once:** adoption also goes through `_setAttr`, so an adopted control gets one property write the first time it's bound. Ticket 07 needs to make the first comparison against the live DOM property.\n- **One combined commit:** the last four checklist items went into a single commit instead of one each.\n- **Port clash:** one test run hit `EADDRINUSE` on port 8123 because another worktree was testing; a retry fixed it.\n\nI also added a paragraph to `AGENTS.md` about the control properties and how to write \"bound value wins\" tests that can actually fail."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274,"cache_read_input_tokens":85673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274},"output_tokens":674,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8132dff8-ba8c-44f6-9a67-86e5bf14ffeb","uuid":"ff1d59e6-f59c-4577-a5e8-870d7934ca8f","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:10:01.692Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NGCmPSnrpyMQeAZ3PA"}
